# The build context admits only what docker/Dockerfile reads: the reactor (the root pom, the own modules and, of the
# submodule uchar/, the RegelSpraak frontend and the Drools backend), bin/regelspraak, docker/ and the served rules
# under examples/. Everything else stays out, the rest of uchar/ included.
*
!pom.xml
!bin/regelspraak
!uchar-frontend/
!toolchain/
!service/
!service-quarkus/pom.xml
!uchar/frontends/regelspraak/
!uchar/backends/drools/
!docker/
!examples/

# Never: git metadata (the repository's .git directory and the .git file the submodule carries), build output of a
# host checkout, the dependency-reduced pom uchar's backend build writes beside its pom, editor and OS files.
.git
uchar/.git
**/.git
**/target/
**/dependency-reduced-pom.xml
**/.DS_Store
